.TH CProgressBar n 03/08/98 "CADC"
.\".BS
.SH NAME
CProgressBar 
\- Create and manipulate a progressBar widget.

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBCProgressBar\fI \fIpathName \fR?\fIoptions\fR?

.SH "INHERITANCE"
itk::Widget \<- LabeledWidget \<- CProgressBar

.SO
\-background	\-cursor	\-foreground
\-font	\-orient
.SE

.SH "INHERITED OPTIONS"
.LP
.nf
.ta 4c 8c 12c
\fB\-clientdata\fR	\fB\-labelimage\fR	\fB\-labeltext\fR	
\fB\-labelbitmap\fR	\fB\-labelmargin\fR	\fB\-labelvariable\fR
\fB\-labelfont\fR	\fB\-labelpos\fR	
.fi
.LP
See the "labeledwidget" class manual entry for details on the 
inherited options.

.SH "WIDGET-SPECIFIC OPTIONS"

.OP \-busycolor busyColor Color
Specifies the trough color of the scale component when the progress
bar is busy.  The default color is blue.

.OP \-digits digits Digits
This option pertains to the scale component, see the Tk
\fBscale\fR widget.

.OP \-from from From
This option pertains to the scale component, see the Tk
\fBscale\fR widget.

.OP \-idlecolor idleColor Color
Specifies the trough color of the scale component when the progress
bar is idle.  The default color is grey.

.OP \-length length Length
This option pertains to the scale component, see the Tk
\fBscale\fR widget.

.OP \-showvalue showValue ShowValue
Specifies whether or not the value is shown.  These values are
the "from", "to",  and current value.  The value may have any
of the forms accepted by Tcl_GetBoolean.  The default value
is false.

.OP \-sliderlength sliderLength SliderLength
This option pertains to the scale component, see the Tk
\fBscale\fR widget.

.OP \-speed speed Speed
Specifies the value's rate of increase, in milliseconds, when 
the progress bar is busy.   The default value is 250 milliseconds.

.OP \-to to To
Specifies the end value.  This is a real value.

.OP \-value value Value
Specifies the progress bar's current value.  This causes the 
position of the slider to change and the current value displayed
is updated.  This is a numerical value. 

.OP \-valueforeground valueForeground Foreground
Specifies the normal foreground color of the value display area.
The default color is black.

.OP \-variable variable Variable
This option pertains to the scale component, see the Tk
\fBscale\fR widget.

.OP \-width width Width
This option pertains to the scale component, see the Tk
\fBscale\fR widget.
.\".BE

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBCProgressBar\fR command creates a new window (given by the
\fIpathName\fR argument) and makes it into a progressBar widget.
Additional options, described above, may be specified on the 
command line or in the option database to configure aspects of
the progressBar. The \fBCProgressBar\fR command returns its
\fIpathName\fR argument.  At the time this command is invoked,
there must not exist a window named \fIpathName\fR, but
\fIpathName\fR's parent must exist.
.PP
The \fBCProgressBar\fR command creates a scale widget and a
display area.  The progress bar is intended usage is to indicate
the progress of some action.  However, it can also be used as
a thermometer.

.SH "WINDGET COMMAND"
The \fBCProgressBar\fR command creates a new Tcl command whose
name is \fIpathName\fR.  This
command may be used to invoke various
operations on the widget.  It has the following general form:
.CS
\fIpathName method \fR?\fIarg arg ...\fR?
.CE
\fIMethod\fR and the \fIarg\fRs
determine the exact behavior of the command.  
.PP
The following methods are possible for CProgressBar widgets:

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcget\fR \fIoption\fR
Returns the current value of the configuration option given
by \fIoption\fR.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCProgressBar\fR
command.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBchildsite\fR
Return the path name of the child site, the child site contains
all of the check buttons.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBcomponent\fR ?\fIname\fR? ?\fIcommand arg arg ...\fR?
Used to query or access component widgets within the progressBar
widget.  For example each of the check buttons is a component of
the progressBar widget.  With no arguments, this returns a list of
symbolic names for component widgets that are accessible in the
current scope.  
.sp
If a symbolic \fIname\fR is specified this method returns the window
path name for that component.
.sp
Otherwise, the \fIcommand\fR and any remaining \fIarg\fR arguments
are invoked as a method on the component with the symbolic \fIname\fR.
This provides a well-defined mechanism for accessing internal components
without relying on specific window path names.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBconfig\fR
See \fBconfigure\fI.

.TP
\fIpathName\fR \fBconfigure\fR ?\fIoption\fR? ?\fIvalue option value ...\fR?
Query or modify the configuration options of the widget.
If no \fIoption\fR is specified, returns a list describing all of
the available options for \fIpathName\fR (see \fBTk_ConfigureInfo\fR for
information on the format of this list).  If \fIoption\fR is specified
with no \fIvalue\fR, then the command returns a list describing the
one named option (this list will be identical to the corresponding
sublist of the value returned if no \fIoption\fR is specified).  If
one or more \fIoption\-value\fR pairs are specified, then the command
modifies the given widget option(s) to have the given value(s);  in
this case the command returns an empty string.
\fIOption\fR may have any of the values accepted by the \fBCProgressBar\fR
command.
.TP
\fIpathName \fBdoSomething\fR \fIindex\fR
Makes the progress bar appears as if it whatever it is monitoring
is doing something.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBisa\fR \fBclassName\fR
Sets the CProgressBar's class to the specified class name.

.TP
\fIpathName \fBlookBusy\fR ?\fBboolVal\fR?
Make the progress bar portray activity, or stop portraying
activity.
If the \fIboolVal\fR is "true" then it portrays activity, and 
not active if it is
false. The slider is incremented by 1 every time interval when
the progress bar is looking busy.  The time interval used
is the value given by the \fI\-speed\fR option.  Any boolean
value accepted by \fBTcl_GetBoolean\fR may be given. The default
value is "true".

.TP
\fIpathName \fBreset\fR ?\fIlabelText\fR?
This method resets the progress bar's value back to the value
specified by the \fI-to\fR option.  It also changes the
text of the progress bar's label to the string value given.  If no
value is given then the label will contain no text.

.SH "COMPONENTS"
.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBfrom\fR
Class:  \fBLabel\fR
.fi
.IP
This component contains the "from" value that is displayed when a
"true" boolean value is specified by the \-show option.  See
the \fBlabel\fR manual entry for more information.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBfvFrame\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
This component is the filler between the from and value labels.  
This frame is used to ensure the value is positioned where the
scale value is positioned. See the \fBframe\fR manual entry for
more information.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBscale\fR
Class:  \fBScale\fR
.fi
.IP
This component is the scale (progress bar) used to indicate the progress.
See the \fBscale\fR manual entry for more information.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBto\fR
Class:  \fBLabel\fR
.fi
.IP
This component contains the "to" value that is displayed when a
"true" boolean value is specified by the \-show option.  See
the \fBlabel\fR manual entry for more information.


.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBvalue\fR
Class:  \fBlabel\fR
.fi
.IP
This component contains the bar value that is displayed when a
"true" boolean value is specified by the \-show option.  See
the \fBlabel\fR manual entry for more information.


.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBvalueFrame\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
This component contains the from, to, and bar values.
See the \fBframe\fR manual entry for more information.

.LP
.nf
Name:   \fBvtFrame\fR
Class:  \fBFrame\fR
.fi
.IP
This component is the filler between the value and to labels.  
This frame is used to ensure the value is positioned where the
scale value is positioned. See the \fBframe\fR manual entry for
more information.


.SH "DEFAULT BINDINGS"
.PP
No bindings are defined for this widget except those defined for the
various components this widget is comprised of.
.PP
See the \fBscale\fR, \fBlabel\fR, and \fBframe\fR
manual entries for more information.


.SH EXAMPLE
.DS
 CProgressBar .p -busy color red -orient horizontal 	\\
	    -speed 350 -to 100 
 pack .p -fill x -expand yes
 .p configure -labelText "Formatting hard drive..."
 .p lookBusy 1
.DE

.SH AUTHOR
Shannon Jaeger

.SH KEYWORDS
progress bar, widget
